---
import AffiliateLink from "../components/AffiliateLink.astro";
import Simple from "../layouts/Simple.astro";
---
<Simple
  title="Affiliate disclosure"
  description="metricspick earns a commission on some DataFast subscriptions. The link uses via=sortino, the price is not higher, and other tools are reviewed without an affiliate program."
  kicker="Disclosure"
  lede="If a link goes to datafa.st, it is an affiliate link. The parameter is via=sortino. You do not pay extra if you subscribe."
  crumbs={[{ href: "/", label: "Home" }, { label: "Affiliate disclosure" }]}
>
  <p>metricspick participates in DataFast’s affiliate program. Links to datafa.st, including links to documentation and the homepage, include <code>via=sortino</code>. If you start a paid DataFast subscription through one of those links, we may earn a commission. DataFast’s own pages describe the customer price. The commission is not added on top.</p>
  <p>A typical link looks like this: <AffiliateLink placement="disclosure-page">datafa.st with our affiliate parameter</AffiliateLink>. Deeper pages keep the same parameter, for example the cookieless-tracking doc. Each affiliate link is marked <code>rel="sponsored"</code> and opens in a new tab.</p>
  <p>We do not run affiliate programs for Google Analytics, PostHog, Mixpanel, Amplitude, Plausible, or Fathom in this version of the site. Those products are still compared, and a page can recommend one of them when the job calls for it. The DataFast recommendation is limited to revenue attribution. It is not a claim that DataFast replaces a product-analytics suite.</p>
  <p>Clicks on datafa.st links are recorded in a <code>dataLayer</code> array in your browser, with the link URL, the link text, the page path, and a placement name. Google Tag Manager container <code>GTM-PJ8GQK6B</code> can read that event. Details are on the <a href="/privacy/">privacy</a> page.</p>
  <p>Editorial pages are not for sale. A vendor cannot pay to rewrite a con, delete a price, or change a job-to-be-done. The method is on <a href="/how-we-test/">how we test</a>. The <a href="/reviews/datafast/">DataFast review</a> repeats this disclosure near the top of the page, as do the other money pages.</p>
</Simple>
